WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:01:53.520 --> 00:01:55.430
I knew it. An undersea volcano.

3
00:01:55.440 --> 00:01:55.910
Straight ahead.

4
00:01:55.920 --> 00:01:57.100
[USOPP, CHOPPER, BROOK, FRANKY]
– What?
– What?

5
00:01:57.120 --> 00:01:59.050
Looks like it's about to blow!

6
00:02:00.400 --> 00:02:02.790
[DECKEN]
Pull back, men!

7
00:02:02.800 --> 00:02:04.840
We'll live to
plunder another day!

8
00:02:04.850 --> 00:02:06.380
[FLYING PIRATES yell]
[FLYING PIRATE A]
– Roger!

9
00:02:06.410 --> 00:02:07.680
You don't gotta ask me twice!

10
00:02:07.690 --> 00:02:08.170
[DECKEN]
Ankoro!

11
00:02:08.190 --> 00:02:08.790
Wadatsumi!

12
00:02:08.810 --> 00:02:10.040
Draw the ship!

13
00:02:11.080 --> 00:02:14.430
Okay, Captain, sure!

14
00:02:14.490 --> 00:02:15.200
[DECKEN]
Vander Decken is my name,

15
00:02:15.210 --> 00:02:17.420
and these long-lost
riches, I'll get later!

16
00:02:17.430 --> 00:02:18.880
[FLYING PIRATES]
– Yeah!
– Yeah!

17
00:02:19.910 --> 00:02:21.550
Oh, no!

18
00:02:21.590 --> 00:02:23.880
Luffy, I don't know
how the Kraken works,

19
00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:26.970
but order him to turn
around and haul ass!

20
00:02:26.980 --> 00:02:28.990
Hey, Surume!

21
00:02:29.030 --> 00:02:30.430
Wait a sec.

22
00:02:31.980 --> 00:02:34.690
[USOPP]
He's hauling ass
just fine all on his own.

23
00:02:34.880 --> 00:02:37.590
For such a giant monster,
it's kind of shameful, actually.

24
00:02:37.600 --> 00:02:38.550
Who cares?

25
00:02:38.560 --> 00:02:40.590
I would be doing the same thing!

26
00:02:42.960 --> 00:02:44.530
He runs terribly.

27
00:02:44.560 --> 00:02:45.670
Give him a break!

28
00:02:45.680 --> 00:02:48.850
I'd rather be clumsy and alive
than graceful and dead!

29
00:02:48.860 --> 00:02:50.830
Like... me?

30
00:02:50.870 --> 00:02:52.590
What the hell is
mouth brow doing?

31
00:02:52.600 --> 00:02:55.280
Whoo! Yeah! Baby!

32
00:02:55.300 --> 00:02:56.750
It's rehab!

33
00:03:00.440 --> 00:03:02.730
Come on! I wanna see lava!

34
00:03:02.920 --> 00:03:05.230
[USOPP]
Evacuate to the
front of the ship!

35
00:03:05.240 --> 00:03:06.250
[CHOPPER]
Hurry!

36
00:03:06.280 --> 00:03:07.630
[NAMI]
That's not gonna help!

37
00:03:07.640 --> 00:03:10.040
It's just a couple of feet!

38
00:03:12.840 --> 00:03:15.000
[ALL scream]

39
00:03:16.650 --> 00:03:24.040
[ALL screaming]
[LUFFY laughing]

40
00:03:26.870 --> 00:03:29.200
[NAMI]
Well, you got your lava, Luffy.

41
00:03:29.210 --> 00:03:31.510
It's getting hotter.

42
00:03:31.610 --> 00:03:34.880
Nobody told me we could
be boiled alive down here!

43
00:03:34.890 --> 00:03:36.890
The ocean sure hates us!

44
00:03:47.010 --> 00:03:48.210
[USOPP]
If you don't hurry it up,

45
00:03:57.330 --> 00:03:59.000
somebody is gonna be
eating your delicious,

46
00:03:59.010 --> 00:04:01.750
cooked carcass from
off the ocean floor!

47
00:04:04.290 --> 00:04:05.720
[LUFFY]
Ooh, riding him is pretty fun,

48
00:04:05.730 --> 00:04:07.620
but eating him might
be even better!

49
00:04:07.650 --> 00:04:10.420
[roars]

50
00:04:10.450 --> 00:04:11.990
The temperature change–

51
00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:14.390
it's causing a vortex
in the current!

52
00:04:14.400 --> 00:04:17.670
[SANJI]
Nami, which direction
is Fishman Island?

53
00:04:17.680 --> 00:04:18.870
We can't lose our wa–

54
00:04:18.880 --> 00:04:21.500
You're not ready for
real girls yet, Sanji!

55
00:04:21.510 --> 00:04:23.490
Go back to your
pictures and relax!

56
00:04:23.520 --> 00:04:26.020
Straight ahead. I have an idea!

57
00:04:27.750 --> 00:04:29.090
We're getting closer!

58
00:04:33.010 --> 00:04:34.470
Now, jump into the trench!

59
00:04:40.350 --> 00:04:40.850
[CHOPPER yelps]

60
00:04:40.850 --> 00:04:42.150
That doesn't look safe!

61
00:04:42.150 --> 00:04:43.100
[BOTH]
– No!
– No!

62
00:04:45.330 --> 00:04:47.050
That's not a place you jump!

63
00:04:47.050 --> 00:04:49.000
It's an abyss!

64
00:04:49.000 --> 00:04:51.960
[CHOPPER]
Yeah, there's nothing
but blackness down there!

65
00:04:51.960 --> 00:04:55.630
Fish people live there?
They've gotta be insane!

66
00:05:04.430 --> 00:05:08.860
And the void in front of us!
Help! Can't we go up?

67
00:05:08.870 --> 00:05:10.180
Up, where it's not
burning and dark

68
00:05:10.190 --> 00:05:12.260
and everything wants to kill us?

69
00:05:12.270 --> 00:05:12.900
Wait!

70
00:05:12.910 --> 00:05:14.420
You're not really
Luffy, are you?

71
00:05:14.430 --> 00:05:16.240
You're some evil demon
who looks like him

72
00:05:16.270 --> 00:05:18.900
that wants to drag us
to the depths of hell!

73
00:05:18.910 --> 00:05:20.120
This is a nightmare!

74
00:05:20.130 --> 00:05:23.830
– Why can't I wake up? Why?
[LUFFY]
– Surume! Jump in!

75
00:05:31.410 --> 00:05:33.580
[USOPP]
It's erupting again!

76
00:05:35.560 --> 00:05:36.800
Whoa, look above us!

77
00:05:36.800 --> 00:05:38.400
Something's coming down!

78
00:05:39.150 --> 00:05:40.050
[ROBIN]
Boulders?

79
00:05:40.050 --> 00:05:41.070
[BROOK]
A mudslide?

80
00:05:41.070 --> 00:05:43.030
It's an avalanche!
Brace yourselves!

81
00:05:46.090 --> 00:05:47.760
[NAMI]
Dodge the boulders, Surume!

82
00:05:50.910 --> 00:05:53.040
I can't just sit here;
I'm gonna go cut 'em!

83
00:05:54.190 --> 00:05:55.940
Luffy, hold onto my leg, okay?

84
00:05:55.950 --> 00:05:57.420
Sure! Gotcha!

85
00:05:57.450 --> 00:05:58.030
[ZORO grunts]

86
00:05:58.060 --> 00:06:00.560
Zoro! You can't!

87
00:06:00.590 --> 00:06:01.120
What's the big idea?

88
00:06:01.130 --> 00:06:02.000
Yeah, let him go, Robin!

89
00:06:02.020 --> 00:06:04.890
The ship is over 8,000
meters deep right now!

90
00:06:04.900 --> 00:06:05.870
Never mind the boulders,

91
00:06:05.880 --> 00:06:08.680
We just need to buy some time
to get away from the cliff wall!

92
00:06:06.180 --> 00:06:08.490
go outside and the water
pressure will crush you!

93
00:06:08.500 --> 00:06:10.310
Fine, but we gotta do something!

94
00:06:10.500 --> 00:06:11.830
[USOPP]
Leave it to me, then!

95
00:06:11.860 --> 00:06:12.790
[GROUP gasps]

96
00:06:12.820 --> 00:06:16.320
[USOPP]
Special Attack,
Green Star: Sargasso!

97
00:06:21.140 --> 00:06:22.090
It stopped the boulders.

98
00:06:22.100 --> 00:06:24.210
Ah! Usopp made seaweed appear!

99
00:06:24.220 --> 00:06:24.630
Oh, wow! Nice shot!

100
00:06:24.640 --> 00:06:25.140
That's handy!

101
00:06:25.150 --> 00:06:26.040
So awesome!

102
00:06:26.060 --> 00:06:27.970
It won't hold for
very long, though.

103
00:06:27.980 --> 00:06:30.020
We gotta get moving, Surume!

104
00:06:30.220 --> 00:06:31.450
Move it!

105
00:06:38.080 --> 00:06:39.570
[STRAW HATS yell]

106
00:06:39.600 --> 00:06:41.100
[CHOPPER]
Just in time!

107
00:06:41.130 --> 00:06:42.460
[USOPP grunts]

108
00:06:46.300 --> 00:06:49.800
Monster plants?
Aw, man! That's cool!

109
00:06:49.820 --> 00:06:52.760
[BROOK]
I wonder what else you
have in that bag of tricks!

110
00:06:52.780 --> 00:06:53.330
[CHOPPER]
Looks like we're in the clear!

111
00:06:53.340 --> 00:06:55.410
That Nami. So harsh.

112
00:06:55.420 --> 00:06:57.360
[LUFFY]
You were pretty
great, too, Surume!

113
00:06:58.300 --> 00:06:59.040
Thanks a bunch!

114
00:06:59.050 --> 00:07:02.100
[CHOPPER]
Yeah! You saved us all!

115
00:07:02.100 --> 00:07:04.310
[NAMI]
You're the best, Surume!

116
00:07:04.310 --> 00:07:05.800
[STRAW HATS chanting]
– Surume! Yay!
– Surume! Yay!

117
00:07:05.800 --> 00:07:09.810
Surume! Yay! Surume! Yay!

118
00:07:09.810 --> 00:07:10.600
Surume! Yay! Suru–

119
00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:38.090
10,000 METERS BELOW SEA LEVEL "THE DEEP"
(THE BOTTOM OF THE OCEANIC TRENCH)

120
00:07:36.680 --> 00:07:39.390
[BROOK]
Are we alive? Or dead?

121
00:07:39.400 --> 00:07:42.650
There's light, but we're
so deep in the sea.

122
00:07:42.680 --> 00:07:43.900
So bright!

123
00:07:43.910 --> 00:07:45.660
I've got stars in my eyes!

124
00:07:45.670 --> 00:07:48.760
Rather, just stars.
There aren't any eyes.

125
00:07:48.860 --> 00:07:50.030
Nya, ho, ho, ho...

126
00:07:50.070 --> 00:07:51.820
Guys! Check it out!

127
00:07:51.830 --> 00:07:54.020
Over there! I think we made it!

128
00:07:54.030 --> 00:07:54.770
[STRAW HATS]
– Huh?
– Huh?

129
00:07:54.790 --> 00:07:57.800
[USOPP]
I can't see anything.
It's too bright.

130
00:07:58.680 --> 00:07:59.950
C'mon, Nami. Tell us!

131
00:07:59.960 --> 00:08:02.030
[NAMI]
Yep! There's
no doubt about it!

132
00:08:02.040 --> 00:08:04.340
The needle is pointing
straight ahead.

133
00:08:04.520 --> 00:08:06.050
We did it.

134
00:08:07.400 --> 00:08:09.550
[LUFFY]
Fishman Island!

135
00:08:09.560 --> 00:08:11.960
[LUFFY]
It's huge!

136
00:08:11.970 --> 00:08:14.020
[NAMI]
It's in a giant bubble!

137
00:08:14.130 --> 00:08:16.270
It looks like they have clouds!

138
00:08:16.290 --> 00:08:18.530
There must be air inside.

139
00:08:24.080 --> 00:08:26.810
We made it!

140
00:08:26.960 --> 00:08:28.620
The New World is next!

141
00:08:28.630 --> 00:08:29.670
Almost there!

142
00:08:29.680 --> 00:08:31.110
Well, what do ya know.

143
00:08:31.120 --> 00:08:33.790
The morons survived after all!

144
00:08:35.920 --> 00:08:37.970
[SANJI]
This is where the mermaids live.

145
00:08:38.000 --> 00:08:40.310
Real, live, beautiful mermaids!

146
00:08:40.320 --> 00:08:42.310
My dream can finally come true.

147
00:08:42.320 --> 00:08:44.550
How I've longed
to see their faces.

148
00:08:44.560 --> 00:08:45.750
To touch them!

149
00:08:45.760 --> 00:08:48.000
[SANJI, BROOK]
– ♪ A mermaid for me! ♪
– ♪ A mermaid for me! ♪

150
00:08:51.420 --> 00:08:53.000
♪ A mermaid for you! ♪

151
00:08:53.010 --> 00:08:54.760
♪ A mermaid for– ♪

152
00:08:54.770 --> 00:08:56.120
Hold up!

153
00:08:56.130 --> 00:08:57.490
You're not ready for this!

154
00:08:57.500 --> 00:08:58.840
You shouldn't even
think about it!

155
00:08:58.850 --> 00:09:00.540
Sanji!

156
00:09:09.760 --> 00:09:11.030
I'm sorry!

157
00:09:11.120 --> 00:09:13.270
I thought my treatment
would do the trick!

158
00:09:13.280 --> 00:09:14.390
I know it's your dream,

159
00:09:14.400 --> 00:09:16.390
but you're not healthy
enough for mermaids.

160
00:09:16.400 --> 00:09:17.510
Doctor!

161
00:09:17.520 --> 00:09:19.640
For him, this is a fate
worse than death.

162
00:09:19.650 --> 00:09:22.200
There's gotta be
something you can do!

163
00:09:22.210 --> 00:09:24.520
If he sees mermaids,
it will be death!

164
00:09:24.530 --> 00:09:25.890
How cruel.

165
00:09:27.730 --> 00:09:30.050
[SANJI grunts]
I don't care.

166
00:09:30.060 --> 00:09:30.740
Sanji!

167
00:09:30.770 --> 00:09:35.220
I-I don't wanna live in
a world without dreams.

168
00:09:35.230 --> 00:09:38.660
I'd rather die leering
at some hot mermaid tail.

169
00:09:38.670 --> 00:09:40.440
You're the worst!

170
00:09:40.670 --> 00:09:42.560
[SANJI]
Who needs blood?

171
00:09:42.750 --> 00:09:45.080
I have lust to sustain me!

172
00:09:45.090 --> 00:09:45.740
Whoa!

173
00:09:45.770 --> 00:09:47.790
His lechery burns bright!

174
00:09:48.830 --> 00:09:50.230
I'm so hungry!

175
00:09:50.470 --> 00:09:51.900
I bet they fry up all kinds

176
00:09:51.910 --> 00:09:54.300
of yummy deep-sea
monsters down here!

177
00:09:54.310 --> 00:09:58.060
Hey, wipe up that drool
and tell Surume to go.

178
00:09:58.070 --> 00:09:59.740
There's an entrance
around here somewhere

179
00:09:59.750 --> 00:10:00.860
and we've gotta find it.

180
00:10:00.870 --> 00:10:03.430
Guys! We got company!

181
00:10:05.320 --> 00:10:07.230
Why would you allow
these foolish humans

182
00:10:07.240 --> 00:10:09.850
to tell you what to do, Kraken?

183
00:10:09.880 --> 00:10:12.120
[roars]

184
00:10:12.120 --> 00:10:14.120
Well, crap. That's not good.

185
00:10:14.920 --> 00:10:17.000
[NAMI]
Sea monsters! Giant ones!

186
00:10:17.030 --> 00:10:18.720
[ALL scream]

187
00:10:18.740 --> 00:10:26.580
[LUFFY]
Wow, they look
tough! I want one!

188
00:10:18.750 --> 00:10:21.540
So close! And now we're dead!

189
00:10:28.570 --> 00:10:30.570
[LUFFY]
Wait, is somebody riding 'em?

190
00:10:36.660 --> 00:10:38.480
What the heck, Surume?

191
00:10:38.480 --> 00:10:41.080
Seriously, we were almost there!

192
00:10:41.080 --> 00:10:42.560
Forget about all that!

193
00:10:42.560 --> 00:10:45.630
Just hang on! Don't
fall off the ship!

194
00:10:55.520 --> 00:10:59.950
[USOPP yells]
Whoa, it's like a
whole circus of sea monsters!

195
00:10:59.960 --> 00:11:02.890
[HAMMOND]
You guys are the
Straw Hat Pirates, aren't you?

196
00:11:04.280 --> 00:11:06.620
[HAMMOND]
You have quite the reputation.

197
00:11:06.760 --> 00:11:08.830
For starters, you were the ones

198
00:11:08.840 --> 00:11:11.980
who ruined the
Arlong Pirates' plans.

199
00:11:10.960 --> 00:11:12.170
[gasps]

200
00:11:12.200 --> 00:11:16.090
[HAMMOND]
That part makes sense at least.

201
00:11:17.320 --> 00:11:19.550
But for some reason,
two years back,

202
00:11:19.560 --> 00:11:23.460
when Hachi was in trouble,
you stood up for your old enemy.

203
00:11:23.720 --> 00:11:26.270
And then, you clocked one
of the Celestial Dragons

204
00:11:26.280 --> 00:11:29.250
right in his ugly face.

205
00:11:29.270 --> 00:11:30.860
Fisher Tiger happened to do

206
00:11:30.870 --> 00:11:33.100
the exact same thing
and he's the hero

207
00:11:33.110 --> 00:11:35.350
of this entire island.

208
00:11:35.990 --> 00:11:38.120
Fisher Tiger?

209
00:11:37.950 --> 00:11:42.750
THE NEW FISHMAN PIRATES - FIGHTER
HAMMOND

210
00:11:40.480 --> 00:11:43.190
[chuckles]
I'm not sure
what to do with you.

211
00:11:42.920 --> 00:11:48.500
THE NEW FISHMAN PIRATES – ASSASSIN
HYOZO

212
00:11:43.200 --> 00:11:44.630
Tell it to me straight.

213
00:11:44.640 --> 00:11:49.370
Are you supposed to be
our enemies or not?

214
00:11:48.630 --> 00:11:54.800
THE NEW FISHMAN PIRATES - FIGHTER
KASAGON

215
00:11:49.440 --> 00:11:51.640
How about I give you an option?

216
00:11:51.760 --> 00:11:53.590
Enlist under our
banner as members

217
00:11:53.600 --> 00:11:56.700
of the New Fishman
Pirates or else!

218
00:11:56.770 --> 00:12:00.140
"Or else" meaning we
sink you right now.

219
00:12:01.570 --> 00:12:03.910
What'd you say?

220
00:12:04.050 --> 00:12:06.120
[NAMI]
Fuel up, Franky, hurry!

221
00:12:06.130 --> 00:12:08.030
Huh? You got a plan?

222
00:12:08.130 --> 00:12:09.720
You and I both know that Luffy

223
00:12:09.730 --> 00:12:12.030
isn't gonna cooperate
with these guys.

224
00:12:12.240 --> 00:12:14.870
But we're 10,000 meters
underwater right now and if we

225
00:12:14.880 --> 00:12:17.030
try to fight them, we don't
stand a chance of winning,

226
00:12:17.040 --> 00:12:19.500
especially not with
those sea monsters.

227
00:12:19.520 --> 00:12:20.870
So, we have to go!

228
00:12:20.880 --> 00:12:23.190
I need you to use all of
the oxygen we have to make

229
00:12:23.200 --> 00:12:24.870
a giant Coup de Burst
so we can charge

230
00:12:24.880 --> 00:12:26.240
straight into Fishman Island!

231
00:12:26.270 --> 00:12:27.640
[BROOK, CHOPPER gasp]

232
00:12:27.670 --> 00:12:29.580
Whoa, are you kiddin' me?

233
00:12:29.590 --> 00:12:33.390
[NAMI]
We've come way
too far to die here.

234
00:12:33.590 --> 00:12:34.540
I agree.

235
00:12:34.550 --> 00:12:38.120
It's risky, but it's likely our
only chance at surviving this.

236
00:12:38.310 --> 00:12:40.550
If that's the case, I'm gonna
fill it up right away!

237
00:12:41.580 --> 00:12:42.300
Franky! Steer the ship!

238
00:12:42.310 --> 00:12:42.760
[HAMMOND]
Humans aren't that clever.

239
00:12:42.770 --> 00:12:44.380
Everything's gonna
be just super.

240
00:12:44.390 --> 00:12:47.370
Whatever it is,
we can deal with it.

241
00:12:47.420 --> 00:12:49.250
So, have you decided if you want

242
00:12:49.260 --> 00:12:52.390
to be part of our crew,
Straw Hat Luffy?

243
00:12:52.700 --> 00:12:56.750
Yeah, right, you wish! Stupid!

244
00:13:00.060 --> 00:13:01.810
Are you sure about that?

245
00:13:01.820 --> 00:13:03.810
You did hear me say
what will happen

246
00:13:03.820 --> 00:13:05.890
if you refuse, didn't you?

247
00:13:05.900 --> 00:13:08.500
Guess you are the
enemy of the fishmen!

248
00:13:08.720 --> 00:13:12.190
Nothing but filthy human scum!

249
00:13:14.400 --> 00:13:16.230
Bleh! Why would I
wanna work for a big

250
00:13:16.240 --> 00:13:18.540
dumb fish face like you?

251
00:13:18.560 --> 00:13:20.750
[CHOPPER]
Cut it out, Luffy!
You'll make him mad!

252
00:13:20.760 --> 00:13:22.430
That's a real shame.

253
00:13:22.440 --> 00:13:25.980
You won't be seeing
Fishman Island after all.

254
00:13:26.120 --> 00:13:29.090
Get ready to sink, Straw Hats.

255
00:13:29.160 --> 00:13:30.460
Sea Lion!

256
00:13:30.990 --> 00:13:35.510
[roars]

257
00:13:31.500 --> 00:13:33.400
FUEL ROOM

258
00:13:35.560 --> 00:13:37.070
[USOPP grunts]
Alright, filled up
and ready to move!

259
00:13:37.080 --> 00:13:38.680
Franky! You're up!

260
00:13:38.070 --> 00:13:39.190
Roger!

261
00:13:38.830 --> 00:13:39.540
[roaring, growling]

262
00:13:39.560 --> 00:13:41.230
[HAMMOND]
Take them down!

263
00:13:41.240 --> 00:13:42.840
Bring it on!

264
00:13:45.240 --> 00:13:46.170
[growling]

265
00:13:46.200 --> 00:13:47.380
Franky, let's go!

266
00:13:47.390 --> 00:13:50.540
Hey, don't forget,
we got our own lion!

267
00:13:50.550 --> 00:13:53.720
Maybe we can fight some
other time, all right?

268
00:13:53.910 --> 00:13:58.210
Here goes. Coup de Burst!

269
00:14:01.210 --> 00:14:02.360
[BOTH gasp]

270
00:14:02.390 --> 00:14:04.440
Look at 'em go!

271
00:14:11.750 --> 00:14:13.800
[ALL yell]

272
00:14:13.840 --> 00:14:16.780
Can't breathe.
There's no more air.

273
00:14:16.820 --> 00:14:20.510
[grunts]
We're getting squished.

274
00:14:20.550 --> 00:14:23.340
[BROOK gasps]
It's hard to
breathe, and that's not

275
00:14:23.350 --> 00:14:26.820
just because I don't have lungs.

276
00:14:27.030 --> 00:14:30.430
Hang on! We'll make it,
no matter what!

277
00:14:32.630 --> 00:14:34.300
What in the hell?

278
00:14:34.310 --> 00:14:36.380
What's up with that crazy ship?

279
00:14:36.390 --> 00:14:38.380
We're on our way in!

280
00:14:38.390 --> 00:14:41.730
I'll be with you soon,
beautiful mermaids!

281
00:14:47.710 --> 00:14:48.550
[BOTH gasp]

282
00:14:48.590 --> 00:14:49.960
[STRAW HATS scream]

283
00:14:49.990 --> 00:14:51.400
[LUFFY]
We lost the coating!

284
00:14:51.430 --> 00:14:54.460
It got stuck when we
crossed the bubble!

285
00:14:56.390 --> 00:15:00.630
[gasps]
Look up there!
What could it be?

286
00:15:01.030 --> 00:15:04.560
[gasps]
This bubble.
It's a double structure!

287
00:15:04.570 --> 00:15:08.480
A normal ship would crash
because there's nothing but air!

288
00:15:08.490 --> 00:15:10.960
We're about to run
into another bubble!

289
00:15:10.970 --> 00:15:12.930
You guys ready?

290
00:15:12.960 --> 00:15:14.670
[GROUP gasping]

291
00:15:20.210 --> 00:15:21.500
Water?

292
00:15:33.130 --> 00:15:35.600
[NAMI]
This current is really strong!

293
00:15:40.770 --> 00:15:43.230
[CHOPPER]
Help... me...

294
00:15:43.230 --> 00:15:44.730
[BROOK]
Can't breathe.

295
00:15:46.320 --> 00:15:49.160
[SANJI]
Crap. Four of us can't swim.

296
00:15:58.240 --> 00:15:59.910
[ZORO]
Come on. Reach!

297
00:16:03.790 --> 00:16:07.280
[SANJI]
Nami! Robin!

298
00:16:10.380 --> 00:16:13.920
[SANJI]
Dammit. I can't
resist the current!

299
00:16:28.870 --> 00:16:30.780
[HAMMOND]
That's one way to get in.

300
00:16:30.790 --> 00:16:32.590
Pretty reckless, though.

301
00:16:32.790 --> 00:16:34.540
Well, we can still
go in after them

302
00:16:34.550 --> 00:16:36.140
if you want to, Hammond.

303
00:16:36.150 --> 00:16:38.780
No way to know if they're
alive or dead, though. Psh.

304
00:16:38.790 --> 00:16:40.350
Yeah, let's track them down.

305
00:16:41.980 --> 00:16:44.210
We can't let Neptune's
Army get their hands

306
00:16:44.220 --> 00:16:46.130
on them first, now can we?

307
00:16:46.140 --> 00:16:47.570
But before we do anything,

308
00:16:47.580 --> 00:16:50.930
we should go back to Noah
and tell the boss what's up.

309
00:16:50.940 --> 00:16:52.930
I think he'd want
to know that the man

310
00:16:52.940 --> 00:16:56.140
who ruined Arlong's
plan is here.

311
00:16:59.000 --> 00:17:01.500
FISHMAN ISLAND - SEA FLOOR

312
00:17:06.610 --> 00:17:08.120
[ICHIKA]
Hey!

313
00:17:10.950 --> 00:17:12.040
Take a look!

314
00:17:12.070 --> 00:17:12.940
I'll look.

315
00:17:12.950 --> 00:17:13.980
I won't!

316
00:17:13.990 --> 00:17:15.260
Maybe I'll look.

317
00:17:15.270 --> 00:17:17.000
Who cares if I look?

318
00:17:18.790 --> 00:17:20.440
Now he's moving!

319
00:17:20.550 --> 00:17:21.500
He moved!

320
00:17:21.510 --> 00:17:22.940
No, he didn't!

321
00:17:22.950 --> 00:17:24.820
He might've moved.

322
00:17:24.980 --> 00:17:26.790
Who cares if he moved?

323
00:17:26.680 --> 00:17:27.410
[coughs]

324
00:17:27.440 --> 00:17:29.250
[GROUP gasps]

325
00:17:29.280 --> 00:17:31.920
[laughs]

326
00:17:31.860 --> 00:17:32.820
Alright! He's alive!

327
00:17:32.820 --> 00:17:33.860
Thank goodness!

328
00:17:35.370 --> 00:17:36.540
Where am I?

329
00:17:36.980 --> 00:17:39.950
[CAMIE]
Oh, Luffy-chin!

330
00:17:39.960 --> 00:17:42.590
It's been a while, hasn't it?

331
00:17:42.600 --> 00:17:44.670
So, how are you feeling?

332
00:17:44.760 --> 00:17:50.490
Hah! Hey, it's Camie!
It's nice to see you!

333
00:17:51.160 --> 00:17:54.060
Oh, Camie, you've
gotten so lovely!

334
00:17:54.120 --> 00:17:55.000
Marry me!

335
00:17:55.860 --> 00:17:58.540
Then we made it to
Fishman Island after all?

336
00:17:58.580 --> 00:17:59.610
Yeah, we did!

337
00:17:59.620 --> 00:18:01.850
From what I understand,
we were about to drown,

338
00:18:01.860 --> 00:18:04.160
but then we were rescued
by a bunch of mermaids!

339
00:18:04.170 --> 00:18:05.280
That's right!

340
00:18:05.290 --> 00:18:07.860
Sanji, Chopper, and I just
woke up a few minutes ago.

341
00:18:07.870 --> 00:18:09.340
Guess we're pretty lucky, huh?

342
00:18:09.630 --> 00:18:11.780
Lucky enough to wake up
in Camie's house.

343
00:18:11.790 --> 00:18:12.890
Here, catch.

344
00:18:12.990 --> 00:18:15.140
Oh. So, this is your house?

345
00:18:15.150 --> 00:18:17.300
[CAMIE]
My bad! I know I was supposed

346
00:18:17.310 --> 00:18:19.780
to pick you guys up on
Sabaody, but I was thinking

347
00:18:19.790 --> 00:18:21.830
that was another month from now.

348
00:18:22.490 --> 00:18:25.760
Heh. That's okay!
Where is everybody?

349
00:18:25.770 --> 00:18:30.240
Well, uh. Looks like
we got separated.

350
00:18:30.250 --> 00:18:32.620
Goodness. I hope they're safe.

351
00:18:32.810 --> 00:18:34.160
So, they're lost?

352
00:18:34.170 --> 00:18:35.920
Yeah. Before I blacked out,

353
00:18:35.930 --> 00:18:37.930
I was trying to follow
them, but that current

354
00:18:38.210 --> 00:18:40.200
must've pulled them off
in a different direction.

355
00:18:40.210 --> 00:18:41.380
Ah, gotcha.

356
00:18:41.410 --> 00:18:43.640
Well, I'm sure it'll
turn out okay, right?

357
00:18:43.650 --> 00:18:44.600
They're fine.

358
00:18:44.610 --> 00:18:47.000
The bonehead can't
do much underwater,

359
00:18:47.010 --> 00:18:49.650
but the robot and Moss Head
are probably with him.

360
00:18:49.810 --> 00:18:50.610
So, I wouldn't worry.

361
00:18:50.200 --> 00:18:51.210
Right, everything'll
be just fine!

362
00:18:51.220 --> 00:18:53.850
[CAMIE]
I hope I get
to see them again soon.

363
00:18:53.860 --> 00:18:55.350
Anyway, here you go!

364
00:18:55.460 --> 00:18:57.030
I'm sure you're all freezing.

365
00:18:57.060 --> 00:18:59.430
So, I made some soup
that'll warm you right up.

366
00:18:59.460 --> 00:19:00.920
[GROUP cheers]

367
00:19:00.950 --> 00:19:02.140
[CAMIE]
Ta-dah!

368
00:19:02.180 --> 00:19:05.280
Cold seaweed soup! It's yummy!

369
00:19:08.970 --> 00:19:10.450
[USOPP]
It's cold?

370
00:19:10.460 --> 00:19:11.630
[CAMIE]
Mm-hm!

371
00:19:11.630 --> 00:19:14.590
[screams]

372
00:19:14.590 --> 00:19:16.180
That's not right,
how are you supposed

373
00:19:16.180 --> 00:19:19.300
to get warm if the soup
is cold? I'm sorry!

374
00:19:19.300 --> 00:19:20.720
Wha...?

375
00:19:20.720 --> 00:19:23.060
I'm such a failure!

376
00:19:23.090 --> 00:19:25.360
[BOTH screaming]

377
00:19:25.390 --> 00:19:28.770
But your soup is great, Camie.

378
00:19:28.770 --> 00:19:31.860
I'm warmer already!

379
00:19:31.860 --> 00:19:33.570
[CHOPPER]
That doesn't make sense.

380
00:19:33.570 --> 00:19:35.360
Come on, let me try some too!

381
00:19:38.170 --> 00:19:40.000
Your clothes are dry, everybody!

382
00:19:40.010 --> 00:19:40.960
They're dry!

383
00:19:40.970 --> 00:19:42.640
No, they're not dry!

384
00:19:42.650 --> 00:19:44.160
Your clothes might be dry.

385
00:19:44.170 --> 00:19:46.270
Who cares if they're dry?

386
00:19:49.460 --> 00:19:50.700
Ah!

387
00:19:50.730 --> 00:19:52.730
[LUFFY]
You took care
of our clothes, too?

388
00:19:52.740 --> 00:19:54.000
Wow, thanks!

389
00:19:54.030 --> 00:19:55.560
[laughs]

390
00:19:55.590 --> 00:19:57.650
[LUFFY]
Who are those little guys?

391
00:19:57.750 --> 00:19:59.750
[CAMIE]
Oh, they're
some friends of mine.

392
00:19:59.830 --> 00:20:01.500
The Medaka Mermaid Quintuplets.

393
00:20:01.510 --> 00:20:02.590
I'm Ichika!

394
00:20:02.630 --> 00:20:03.460
I'm Nika!

395
00:20:03.470 --> 00:20:04.380
I'm Sanka!

396
00:20:04.410 --> 00:20:05.310
I'm Yonka!

397
00:20:05.350 --> 00:20:06.940
And I'm Yonka Two!

398
00:20:06.950 --> 00:20:09.250
[USOPP]
Wait, why are there two Yonkas?

399
00:20:09.260 --> 00:20:12.110
They're really fast swimmers,
and pretty clever as well!

400
00:20:12.140 --> 00:20:14.290
Yeah? Nice to meet ya!

401
00:20:14.300 --> 00:20:16.940
I've got a lot of neat
friends here, actually.

402
00:20:16.940 --> 00:20:19.010
This is the sea floor
of the Mermaid Cove,

403
00:20:19.020 --> 00:20:21.290
home to the girls' dorm
of the famous Mermaid Café!

404
00:20:21.320 --> 00:20:22.600
[SANJI]
Huh?

405
00:20:22.340 --> 00:20:23.710
[BOTH gasp]
Uh-oh!

406
00:20:22.610 --> 00:20:24.130
G-G-G-The girls' dorm?

407
00:20:24.130 --> 00:20:25.480
Please, Camie!

408
00:20:25.490 --> 00:20:28.720
Tell me everything about
this Mermaid Café place!

409
00:20:28.770 --> 00:20:30.440
Oh, it's just this
cute little café

410
00:20:30.450 --> 00:20:31.960
where I work as a waitress.

411
00:20:31.970 --> 00:20:34.500
We have a lot of pretty
mermaids there on staff.

412
00:20:35.490 --> 00:20:38.620
Ah! Sounds like heaven!

413
00:20:39.260 --> 00:20:41.930
Can I get you anything extra?

414
00:20:44.330 --> 00:20:45.310
Sanji!

415
00:20:45.340 --> 00:20:47.110
Don't die!

416
00:20:47.900 --> 00:20:48.820
I won't die!

417
00:20:48.830 --> 00:20:50.040
[USOPP, CHOPPER]
– False alarm!
– False alarm!

418
00:20:50.060 --> 00:20:53.700
I swore. I made
a promise to myself,

419
00:20:54.440 --> 00:20:58.240
that for the entire time
I was on Fishman Island

420
00:20:58.280 --> 00:21:01.450
I wouldn't get a
nosebleed and pass out!

421
00:21:03.240 --> 00:21:05.740
[SANJI]
And I've held out for this long,

422
00:21:05.880 --> 00:21:08.810
so I deserve a reward, right?

423
00:21:09.000 --> 00:21:11.120
Pathetic.

424
00:21:11.130 --> 00:21:13.760
[CAMIE]
I know! Why don't
we go up there now?

425
00:21:13.770 --> 00:21:16.610
I'll introduce you
to all of my friends!

426
00:21:19.770 --> 00:21:21.280
[LUFFY]
Whoa! A turtle!

427
00:21:20.980 --> 00:21:23.230
SEA TURTLE
ELEVATOR

428
00:21:21.290 --> 00:21:23.790
[CHOPPER]
"Sea Turtle Elevator," huh?

429
00:21:25.340 --> 00:21:27.540
[CAMIE]
Could you give
us a lift, Mr. Turtle?

430
00:21:27.570 --> 00:21:31.020
[whistle blows]

431
00:21:32.860 --> 00:21:35.250
[CAMIE]
This is a coral
apartment complex.

432
00:21:35.260 --> 00:21:37.990
The dorms are at the very
bottom, so rent's cheap.

433
00:21:38.050 --> 00:21:39.730
The top floor's
the most expensive

434
00:21:39.740 --> 00:21:41.550
because it gets natural light.

435
00:21:41.580 --> 00:21:44.380
[LUFFY]
Mm... Does that
mean you're poor?

436
00:21:44.460 --> 00:21:46.830
And what about
Hachi and Pappagu?

437
00:21:47.180 --> 00:21:49.650
[CAMIE]
Hatchin got beat up
real bad about a year ago.

438
00:21:49.660 --> 00:21:51.250
Oh, yeah, I heard about that.

439
00:21:51.260 --> 00:21:54.370
He was protecting the Sunny
for us back on Sabaody, right?

440
00:21:54.380 --> 00:21:56.350
Hatchin came from
the Fishman District,

441
00:21:56.360 --> 00:21:58.350
so that's where he's been
resting and recovering.

442
00:21:58.360 --> 00:22:00.110
I haven't had the chance
to see him lately,

443
00:22:00.120 --> 00:22:02.350
but from what I hear, he's
getting better all the time.

444
00:22:02.360 --> 00:22:04.740
Huh? He's okay?

445
00:22:04.750 --> 00:22:07.290
Yeah, but it's kind of
a rough part of town.

446
00:22:07.390 --> 00:22:09.310
If you guys go along
with me, I wouldn't mind

447
00:22:09.320 --> 00:22:10.700
heading over there
to visit him, though.

448
00:22:10.710 --> 00:22:11.740
[LUFFY]
Let's do it!

449
00:22:11.750 --> 00:22:14.060
I've been wanting to
thank him face-to-face.

450
00:22:14.070 --> 00:22:16.040
Sure, you got it!

451
00:22:16.150 --> 00:22:19.420
And, well, as for Pappagu...

452
00:22:19.430 --> 00:22:21.970
He's a super-famous
fashion designer.

453
00:22:22.070 --> 00:22:23.980
So, he lives in a
big fancy mansion

454
00:22:23.990 --> 00:22:27.720
in the high-class district
of Fishverly Hills!

455
00:22:27.730 --> 00:22:29.480
I'm supposed to
deliver some clams

456
00:22:29.490 --> 00:22:31.400
over there today.
You wanna come with me?

457
00:22:31.410 --> 00:22:33.320
Wait, he's your pet.

458
00:22:33.330 --> 00:22:35.540
But you two don't live
in the same place?

459
00:22:35.650 --> 00:22:38.680
[giggles]
Yeah, 'cause
that area's a little

460
00:22:38.690 --> 00:22:40.310
out of my price range.

461
00:22:40.320 --> 00:22:43.060
We have better
clams here, anyway.

462
00:22:43.120 --> 00:22:45.160
[CHOPPER]
We're almost to the top!

463
00:22:45.360 --> 00:22:47.670
Huh? Hey, what's that
drinking-straw

464
00:22:47.680 --> 00:22:48.950
looking tube dealie?

465
00:22:49.040 --> 00:22:52.230
Oh. That thing?
That's the Water Road.

466
00:22:52.240 --> 00:22:53.830
The bubble craftsmen built it.

467
00:22:53.840 --> 00:22:56.050
And when mermaids or
fish get inside it...

468
00:22:56.060 --> 00:22:59.430
Well, hold on.
Here, let me show you.

469
00:23:05.580 --> 00:23:08.580
It's the surface! We made it!

470
00:23:08.590 --> 00:23:11.020
Luffy-chin!

471
00:23:13.280 --> 00:23:14.620
[CAMIE]
Look! I'm swimming in the sky!

472
00:23:14.630 --> 00:23:16.060
[GROUP]
– Whoa!
[LUFFY]
– I wanna do that!

473
00:23:16.080 --> 00:23:17.250
Wait a sec!

474
00:23:20.480 --> 00:23:23.880
If we're underwater, why do
I see a sky full of clouds?

475
00:23:23.890 --> 00:23:24.410
No way! I don't get it,
but it sure is neat!

476
00:23:24.420 --> 00:23:26.040
Hey! Camie!

477
00:23:26.040 --> 00:23:26.490
[SANJI, LUFFY]
– Huh?
– Huh?

478
00:23:26.500 --> 00:23:27.680
[SANJI]
Huh? It's a girl!

479
00:23:27.380 --> 00:23:28.630
Where's that coming from?

480
00:23:28.090 --> 00:23:28.570
Whoa.

481
00:23:28.580 --> 00:23:30.810
[gasps]
Hey, guys!

482
00:23:30.820 --> 00:23:32.450
Are these your pirate friends?

483
00:23:34.500 --> 00:23:37.340
I guess that means they
didn't drown after all!

484
00:23:36.230 --> 00:23:37.330
[SANJI whimpers]

485
00:23:37.350 --> 00:23:38.950
You didn't come in
through the entrance

486
00:23:40.710 --> 00:23:43.240
like you're supposed to,
so we were concerned.

487
00:23:42.830 --> 00:23:45.320
[SANJI whimpering]

488
00:23:45.350 --> 00:23:46.540
Well, hi there.

489
00:23:46.550 --> 00:23:48.700
You're not as scary
as I thought you'd be.

490
00:23:48.710 --> 00:23:50.140
So, you broke in?

491
00:23:50.150 --> 00:23:53.230
That's pretty hot. I kinda
have a thing for pirates.

492
00:23:53.260 --> 00:23:57.490
[laughs]
It's like a
real-life fairy tale!

493
00:24:05.500 --> 00:24:09.930
A coral paradise! A whole
cove full of mermaids!

494
00:24:19.970 --> 00:24:23.210
[sobs]

495
00:24:23.240 --> 00:24:24.450
[GROUP gasps]

496
00:24:24.480 --> 00:24:26.350
What's the matter
with Sanji now?

497
00:24:26.380 --> 00:24:29.470
He didn't even cry this hard
when he left the Baratie.

498
00:24:32.230 --> 00:24:35.590
Finally!

499
00:24:35.630 --> 00:24:39.330
I found my All Blue
after all these years!

500
00:24:41.150 --> 00:24:44.740
Are you sure about that? Really?

501
00:24:44.750 --> 00:24:47.130
Here, let me
introduce everybody!

502
00:24:47.140 --> 00:24:49.430
That's Luffy-chin,
he's the captain!

503
00:24:49.710 --> 00:24:51.680
Yeah, nice to meet ya!

504
00:24:51.690 --> 00:24:53.370
[CAMIE]
Sanji-chin's the crybaby.

505
00:24:53.380 --> 00:24:55.530
The nose guy is Usopp-chin!

506
00:24:55.540 --> 00:24:56.790
That's me!

507
00:24:57.140 --> 00:24:59.410
[CAMIE]
And the raccoon
is Chopper-chin!

508
00:24:59.540 --> 00:25:00.780
Not again!

509
00:25:00.810 --> 00:25:01.820
[SANJI whimpering]

510
00:25:01.850 --> 00:25:05.750
[MERMAID]
Aw, why are you crying?

511
00:25:05.850 --> 00:25:06.880
Come over here.

512
00:25:06.890 --> 00:25:08.990
Let's dance in
the water together!

513
00:25:09.020 --> 00:25:11.760
[yells]

514
00:25:14.030 --> 00:25:16.310
Okay. I get it.

515
00:25:16.350 --> 00:25:19.280
This is obviously
too good to be true.

516
00:25:19.390 --> 00:25:22.100
Maybe... I'm destined
to die today.

517
00:25:22.110 --> 00:25:23.380
That's dark!

518
00:25:23.390 --> 00:25:24.580
What the heck happened to you

519
00:25:24.590 --> 00:25:27.000
in the last two years
to make you this gloomy?

520
00:25:27.010 --> 00:25:30.020
Isn't this supposed to be
the land of your dreams?

521
00:25:31.810 --> 00:25:34.040
[LUFFY laughs]
You crack me up, Sanji!

522
00:25:34.050 --> 00:25:36.120
[USOPP, CHOPPER]
– I don't think he's joking!
– I don't think he's joking!

523
00:25:44.070 --> 00:25:46.130
Interesting.

524
00:25:46.140 --> 00:25:49.980
So, Straw Hat finally
made it to our turf, did he?

525
00:25:48.700 --> 00:25:50.400
FISHMAN DISTRICT [NOAH]

526
00:25:49.990 --> 00:25:51.150
Good for him.

527
00:25:52.140 --> 00:25:53.600
[gasps]
Right.

528
00:25:53.610 --> 00:25:56.480
Wh-What are we gonna
do about it, Boss?

529
00:25:58.970 --> 00:26:03.740
[HODY]
I want you to bring
him here, and quickly.
